    "title": "Fuel leak from Chesterfield 7-Eleven closes part of Robious Road - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jessie Nguyen ,\n15 hours ago\nCHESTERFIELD COUNTY, Va. (WRIC) — Officials are urging Chesterfield County residents to avoid part of Robious Road after it was closed due to a fuel leak.\nAt around 9 a.m. on Wednesday, March 11, Chesterfield County Fire and EMS took to social media to warn residents of an oil leak on Robious Road.\nPer the post, the eastbound lanes of Robious Road between Old Bon Air Road and Midlothian Turnpike have been closed.\n(Chesterfield County Fire and EMS) (Chesterfield County Fire and EMS) (Chesterfield County Fire and EMS) (Chesterfield County Fire and EMS) Firefighters and crews with the Hazmat team are on scene working to contain the spill, which officials said was leaking out of a pump at a 7-Eleven gas station.\nRubious Road is expected to be closed for “an extended period of time,” per officials.\nThis is a developing story, stay with 8News for updates.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WRIC ABC 8News.\n1",
    "summary": "CHESTERFIELD COUNTY, Va. (WRIC) — Officials are urging Chesterfield County residents to avoid part of Robious Road after it was closed due to a fuel leak. At around 9 a.m. on Wednesday, March 11, Chesterfield County Fire and EMS took to social media to warn residents of an oil leak on Robious Road.",
